ing asgard now when thor  gets back to new asgard and helps defend  them from these creatures natalie  portman's the mighty thor shows up of  course taking arthor by big surprise  here as she's able to wield mjolnir now  he then goes to what looks to be some  type of a town hall we've seen a scene  where valkyrie is here talking to other  political figures but in this new shot  thor is there giving a speech to what  looks to be a bunch of asgardians so i'm  assuming that this is on asgard  somewhere since he's given the speech to  them and he's trying to get them to  unite and not be afraid of gore the  godbutcher and as korg and thor talk  meek is there writing everything down  that they say if you take a look at the  whiteboard that meek is writing on it is  literally word for word what korg and  thor have said and meek even drew a  little picture of mjolnir on it he drew  the old asgard where everybody came from  and some stars and some lightning also  in this new footage we see a very  interesting structure in the sky which  i'm actually assuming is olympus if you  take a look at it it's all gold like  olympus is it's floating in the sky  perhaps some place over earth but is  shielded so you can't see it i'm  assuming that it does exist in another  realm but is pretty close to earth  because in greek mythology the gods  interact with the earthly humans a lot  and if you take a look at the middle of  this structure it does look like the  place where thor jane foster korg and  the rest of the crew are walking through  in previous trailers remember olympus in  the mcu is going to kind of be like a  city in the sky which is exactly what  this looks like we can also see thor's  goats pulling a chariot with them as  they leave and we can also see the  bifrost i'm assuming that thor jane  foster and everybody else is inside this  chariot and they're using the bifrost to  go explore different parts of the  universe to try and find gore or at  least go back to new asgard we then have  another new scene of the guardians of  the galaxy and drax is yelling he's  yelling as he comes out of the water he  seems to be cutting some vines off of a  creature off of him we see nebula in the  background on the left we see rocket  raccoon in the background on the right  and we see craglin on the left as well  and it looks like he has something stuck  in his nose and on the back of his head  maybe he was attacked somehow in this  scene it does look like they're under  attack and perhaps something got him  right in the nose he does seem to be  screaming and it might be from the pain  unfortunately now i'm not assuming any  guardians are going to die in this of  course that's all going to be left for  guardians of the galaxy vol 3 but i am  really excited to see thor interact with  the guardians even more now the last  thing i want to talk about seems like  it's going to be a pretty important  scene it's of thor and he seems to be in  the same hall that we saw jane foster's  thor in the one that has the statues of  all of the cosmic entities we've only  seen jane foster in this hall before but  as we see here thor is here and in the  background is the watcher and right  behind him we know is the living  tribunal however what really caught my  eye is that to his right there seems to  be another column where there would be  another statue and we know that on the  left side are other cosmic entities as  well so this seems to be a big chamber  or hall dedicated to gods and these  cosmic entities might be considered gods  as well because it looks like some of  them are destroyed in this scene on  thor's right that column seems to be in  rubble it looks a little destroyed and  i'm assuming at one point in time gore  the god butcher went there and destroyed  the faces of some of the gods that he's  killed this might be how gore the god  butcher is kind of keeping tabs on all  of the gods every time he kills a god he  goes to this chamber and he blows up 